    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -4355.777871578612,
        3458.3651572701865
      ],
      "size": [
        1020.9501205596762,
        639.8268833555353
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 4,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MARKDKBERRY.com\n\n*This is a straight upscaler to fix images. It doesnt use the VL to make a prompt from the original image*\n\n- 2mp to test only takes a few mins on 8 steps with a turbo lora. \n- 3mp took 144 seconds for 16:9\n- 4mp took 200 seconds for 16:9\n\n\n## LORAS\n\n\n\n\n## PROMPTS\n\n`upscale <image 1> to make it high detail, realistic. Maintain the likeness of the character as much as possible`\n\n`in image 1 create a full length photograph of the woman in image 2 wearing a blue silk nightgown, barefoot, looking directly at the camera with a neutral expression. no strong shadows. white background. use image 3 and image 4 to define the face.`\n\n`remove the man and horse from the image and replace it with the same man and horse but galloping fast across the same background scene`\n\n`remove the woman from image 1 and replace her with the woman from image 2 looking through binoculars at the camera.`\n\n`Replace the woman in image 1 with the woman from image 2. She is looking through a pair of binoculars, holding them up to her eyes with both hands. Keep her face, hair, clothing and skin tone consistent with image 2. Replace the man reading a book inside the tent in image 1 with the man from image 3, lying in the same position and looking at a book. Keep his face, hair, build and clothing consistent with image 3. Preserve the rest of image 1 exactly as it is: the background, tent, lighting, shadows, color grading, camera angle and composition. Match the lighting and scale of both new people to the scene so they blend in naturally.` \n   - (this also had some negatives: `blurry, distorted face, extra limbs, deformed hands, mismatched lighting, changed background, duplicate people, low quality, artifacts`)\n\n`create a realistic photograph in image 1 using the scene from image 2 of a realistic photograph of a solitary orange and beige pyramid tent stands in a grassy clearing covered with fallen leaves, surrounded by tall, leafless trees in a forest setting, with a distant gothic mansion house visible through the mist in the background on an overcast morning.`\n   - this is to fix a bad antialised image, you basically give it a blank image size in image 1, and tell it to recreate image 2 in image 1.\n\n`Generate a reverse view (from behind / back view) of the person shown in <image2>, strictly preserving their exact clothing, hairstyle, body build, and distinct accessories from <image2>. Keep the same lighting, color grading, and background/environment as <image2>, showing the back of the subject facing away from the camera in high quality, sharp details, 4k.`\n   - I provided a 1024 x 2048 black image in image 1 and the similar aspect ratio full frontal portrait of a person in image 2"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# MARKDKBERRY.com\n\n*This is a straight upscaler to fix images. It doesnt use the VL to make a prompt from the original image*\n\n- 2mp to test only takes a few mins on 8 steps with a turbo lora. \n- 3mp took 144 seconds for 16:9\n- 4mp took 200 seconds for 16:9\n\n\n## LORAS\n\n\n\n\n## PROMPTS\n\n`upscale <image 1> to make it high detail, realistic. Maintain the likeness of the character as much as possible`\n\n`in image 1 create a full length photograph of the woman in image 2 wearing a blue silk nightgown, barefoot, looking directly at the camera with a neutral expression. no strong shadows. white background. use image 3 and image 4 to define the face.`\n\n`remove the man and horse from the image and replace it with the same man and horse but galloping fast across the same background scene`\n\n`remove the woman from image 1 and replace her with the woman from image 2 looking through binoculars at the camera.`\n\n`Replace the woman in image 1 with the woman from image 2. She is looking through a pair of binoculars, holding them up to her eyes with both hands. Keep her face, hair, clothing and skin tone consistent with image 2. Replace the man reading a book inside the tent in image 1 with the man from image 3, lying in the same position and looking at a book. Keep his face, hair, build and clothing consistent with image 3. Preserve the rest of image 1 exactly as it is: the background, tent, lighting, shadows, color grading, camera angle and composition. Match the lighting and scale of both new people to the scene so they blend in naturally.` \n   - (this also had some negatives: `blurry, distorted face, extra limbs, deformed hands, mismatched lighting, changed background, duplicate people, low quality, artifacts`)\n\n`create a realistic photograph in image 1 using the scene from image 2 of a realistic photograph of a solitary orange and beige pyramid tent stands in a grassy clearing covered with fallen leaves, surrounded by tall, leafless trees in a forest setting, with a distant gothic mansion house visible through the mist in the background on an overcast morning.`\n   - this is to fix a bad antialised image, you basically give it a blank image size in image 1, and tell it to recreate image 2 in image 1.\n\n`Generate a reverse view (from behind / back view) of the person shown in <image2>, strictly preserving their exact clothing, hairstyle, body build, and distinct accessories from <image2>. Keep the same lighting, color grading, and background/environment as <image2>, showing the back of the subject facing away from the camera in high quality, sharp details, 4k.`\n   - I provided a 1024 x 2048 black image in image 1 and the similar aspect ratio full frontal portrait of a person in image 2"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
